        width: 34px;
        height: 34px;
        border-radius: 12px;
      }

      .details p {
        padding: 0 16px 20px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Purrfect basics</p>
      <h1 id="page-title">Cat FAQ</h1>
      <p class="intro">Quick answers for curious humans, new cat parents, and anyone trying to decode their favorite tiny house panther.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-shell" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1">
            <span class="question-title"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">🐾</span>Why do cats knead blankets or people?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-1">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>Kneading is a comforting kitten behavior that often sticks around into adulthood. Cats may knead when they feel relaxed, affectionate, or ready to settle into a cozy spot.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2">
            <span class="question-title"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">🧶</span>How much playtime does a cat need?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-2">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>Most cats benefit from two or three short play sessions each day. Wand toys, puzzle feeders, and chase games help satisfy hunting instincts and reduce boredom.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3">
            <span class="question-title"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">😺</span>Why does my cat slow blink at me?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-3">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>A slow blink is often a sign of trust. You can gently slow blink back to show your cat you are calm and friendly.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4">
            <span class="question-title"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">🍽️</span>Should cats eat only dry food?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-4">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>Not necessarily. Many cats do well with a balanced mix of wet and dry food, depending on health needs, hydration, and preference. Ask a veterinarian for diet advice specific to your cat.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5">
            <span class="question-title"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">🏠</span>How can I make my home more cat-friendly?</span>
            <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="details" id="answer-5">
            <div class="details-inner">
              <p>Offer vertical spaces, scratching posts, clean litter boxes, sunny resting spots, and safe hiding places. Cats feel more confident when they can choose where to perch, scratch, nap, and retreat.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const examples = document.querySelectorAll(".example");

    examples.forEach((example) => {
      const button = example.querySelector(".question");

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const isOpen = example.classList.toggle("is-open");
        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(isOpen));
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
